-- title:
--   A uniform word envelope for the scaled shared reporting bank
-- statement:
--   For natural input size $n$, put $m=\operatorname{inputBits}(n)=\operatorname{Nat.log2}(n)$, $h=\operatorname{microHalf}(m)$, $J=\operatorname{blockCount}(m)$, and $M=2^{2048(m+1)}$. Let $g$ be the scheduled band width. The shared-bank word envelope, specialized to source-length bound $n$, satisfies
--   $$
--   \operatorname{word}(h,J,n,g)\le5000(M+1)^5(n+1)^2+M^{64}.
--   $$
--   The left side includes control values, retained source spans, prefix state, radix keys, packed sorted indices, suffix counts, and switch arithmetic. This gives a bound depending only on input size for the complete numeric requirement of the physical shared-bank constructor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsScales.lean#L215-L290

